        "parms": "# rpnin and nrpnin — parameter messages\nSome settings travel as a series of control changes. Controllers 101 and 100 select a registered parameter (RPN), 99 and 98 a non-registered one (NRPN), and controllers 6 and 38 then write its value, coarse and fine. rpnin and nrpnin follow the series and send each value written, with the parameter number and the channel, right to left.\nThe first argument is the input port, counted from 0; the midiinfo tutorial lists them. A port that cannot be opened, or no keyboard at all, leaves the object silent, and the patch still loads. On Windows a port can be open in one place at a time, so untick it under Settings › MIDI for a patch to hear it. The second argument is a channel, 1-16, or 0 for all.",
        "type": ".text"
      },
