          "x": "640.0",
          "y": "200.0",
          "w": "300"
        },
        "parms": "1. Set the pitch-bend range on a controller that sends it as RPN 0. rpnin sends the value, parameter 0 and the channel. The value is 14 bits: shifting it right by 7 gives the coarse byte, the semitones, and the low 7 bits are the fine byte, the cents.",
        "type": ".text"
      },
      "object 14": {
        "ID": 14,
        "gui": {
          "x": "640.0",
          "y": "320.0",
          "w": "300"
        },
        "parms": "2. A device that writes only the coarse byte moves the value in steps of 128: 12 semitones reads as 1536. The parameters are 0 pitch-bend range, 1 fine tuning, 2 coarse tuning, 3 tuning program and 4 tuning bank.",
        "type": ".text"
      },
      "object 15": {
        "ID": 15,
        "gui": {
          "x": "640.0",
          "y": "460.0",
          "w": "300"
        },
        "parms": "3. nrpnin does the same for a device's own parameters. The parameter number is coarse times 128 plus fine, so 1 and 8 on controllers 99 and 98 read as 136. What each number means is in the device's manual.",
        "type": ".text"
      },
